ord  one of the main reasons i personally  like login.gov  is that it offers a second layer of  security  meaning that you can select one or more  than one  of the methods below you can  receive a security code by text message  or phone call  by using an app on a cell phone computer  or tablet to get the code  use a security key if you already have  one if you're unfamiliar it's a physical  device that often looks like a flash  drive  and sometimes you can plug it directly  into your computer  use your government or military piv card  and last but not least 10 backup codes  are provided that you can print out and  keep in a safe place  once you know the account that you would  like to link  you are ready to begin the final stages  although my example is for login.gov use  the exact same steps to link any of the  partners  third party account  step one log in directly to your ncbi  account  these screens should look familiar step  2  locate your username on the upper right  corner  and click the link which will take you  to your account  settings step 3 locate  the linked accounts box and click change  located on the right but before we move  on  as you can see in my example i have  linked more than one third party option  i like to think of my account as a room  with many doors to enter  linking your account to multiple  third-party options  is great for students staff and faculty  who may have who may be switching  institutions and lose logging  credentials  from the former institution let's move  to step four  type in the third party account that you  will be linking  click the link which will take you to  the website in this case login.gov  and provide credential  congratulations you have linked your  account  you should see a confirmation message  and the account name  appearing in your linked account  to the right you can unlink your account  at any time  by clicking on the red x  this change is easy and necessary  so we can focus on making your ncbi  resource 