 account to  google or  any of the partner third-party party  methods  please do so the login is a type of  personal preference  and it's also dependent on what your  organization allows  okay thanks sherry another question is  our it  locks us out of social media like gmail  and our institution is not part of the  in commons  will we still be able to establish an  account and sign in the new way  absolutely you have the option of  login.gov for example  if your organization does not appear on  the in commons list  you can always ask your organization  system administrator to contact  your respective federation consortium to  become a member  additional information about this can  also be found on our login page  okay thanks sherry uh another question  will login.gov accounts work properly  when going through a library's proxy  yes proxies should work properly  if you find that you're having a login  issue with any of the  party option first attempt to log in  outside of the proxy  to make sure that the arrow is not  within the account  after you confirm the issue is the proxy  please contact your it department for  assistance  if they're unable to assist you have  that person contact the ncbi help desk  and we will work with them directly to  troubleshoot the issue  okay thanks uh next question is  um how can i keep my account content  since i have a direct login  your account information like my  bibliography say searches collections  api keys remain intact  linking your choice of third-party login  option  to your current ncbi account will  provide the access to your current  account  okay thanks sherry so that's all the  questions that we're going to answer  today  live but please um take a look at the  faq  uh after the webinar you know give us a  few days to get these things updated but  we'll have  the other questions answered up there  also you know please  contact us at info if you have any  trouble you know  linking your accounts or anything like  that you can write to the help desk at  ncbi  and that's info ncbi.nlm.nih.gov  so that's the conclusion of the webinar  for today so thanks everybody for coming  please you know keep in touch with us  via the info option  and we'll get you through this just fine  okay thanks

